@startuml diagrama_command_DESPUES
!theme plain
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontSize 11
skinparam classFontName Arial

title Diagrama de Clases - WorkOrderService CON Patrón Command\n(Operaciones encapsuladas como objetos)

' ============================================================================
' CLIENTE (Rutas HTTP)
' ============================================================================
class WorkOrderRoutes {
    -invoker: WorkOrderInvoker
    -commandFactory: WorkOrderCommandFactory
    +postTransitionStatus(req, res)
    +postAssignTechnician(req, res)
    +postRegisterExit(req, res)
    +postAddPhoto(req, res)
}

' ============================================================================
' INVOKER (Invocador)
' ============================================================================
class WorkOrderInvoker {
    -commandHistory: CommandHistoryEntry[]
    --
    +executeCommand(command): WorkOrder
    +undoLastCommand(): WorkOrder
    +getHistory(): CommandHistory[]
    +clearHistory(): void
}

note right of WorkOrderInvoker
  **Invoker (Invocador):**
  - Ejecuta comandos sin conocer
    su implementación
  - Mantiene historial de comandos
  - Permite deshacer operaciones
  - Centraliza logging/auditoría
end note

' ============================================================================
' COMMAND INTERFACE
' ============================================================================
interface IWorkOrderCommand {
    +execute(): WorkOrder
    +getDescription(): string
}

interface IUndoableCommand extends IWorkOrderCommand {
    +undo(): WorkOrder
    +canUndo(): boolean
}

note left of IWorkOrderCommand
  **Command Interface:**
  Contrato que todos los
  comandos deben cumplir.
  
  Cada comando encapsula:
  - La operación a realizar
  - Los parámetros necesarios
  - La validación de reglas
end note

' ============================================================================
' COMANDOS CONCRETOS
' ============================================================================
class TransitionStatusCommand implements IUndoableCommand {
    -repository: IWorkOrderRepository
    -orderId: string
    -toStatus: OrderStatus
    -userId: string
    -previousStatus: OrderStatus
    --
    +execute(): WorkOrder
    +undo(): WorkOrder
    +canUndo(): boolean
    +getDescription(): string
}

class AssignTechnicianCommand implements IUndoableCommand {
    -repository: IWorkOrderRepository
    -orderId: string
    -input: AssignTechnicianInput
    -previousTechnicianId: string
    --
    +execute(): WorkOrder
    +undo(): WorkOrder
    +canUndo(): boolean
    +getDescription(): string
}

class RegisterExitCommand implements IWorkOrderCommand {
    -repository: IWorkOrderRepository
    -orderId: string
    -input: ExitRegisterInput
    --
    +execute(): WorkOrder
    +getDescription(): string
}

class AddPhotoCommand implements IWorkOrderCommand {
    -repository: IWorkOrderRepository
    -orderId: string
    -storagePath: string
    -kind: string
    --
    +execute(): WorkOrder
    +getDescription(): string
}

note bottom of TransitionStatusCommand
  **Concrete Commands:**
  Cada comando encapsula
  una operación específica
  con toda su lógica de
  validación y ejecución.
end note

' ============================================================================
' FACTORY DE COMANDOS
' ============================================================================
class WorkOrderCommandFactory {
    -repository: IWorkOrderRepository
    --
    +createTransitionStatusCommand(orderId, toStatus, userId): TransitionStatusCommand
    +createAssignTechnicianCommand(orderId, input): AssignTechnicianCommand
    +createRegisterExitCommand(orderId, input): RegisterExitCommand
    +createAddPhotoCommand(orderId, storagePath, kind): AddPhotoCommand
}

' ============================================================================
' REPOSITORIO (Receiver)
' ============================================================================
interface IWorkOrderRepository {
    +findById(id): WorkOrderRow
    +transitionStatus(id, from, to, userId): WorkOrderRow
    +assignTechnician(id, technicianId): WorkOrderRow
    +registerExit(id, data): WorkOrderRow
    +addPhoto(workOrderId, storagePath, kind): void
}

note bottom of IWorkOrderRepository
  **Receiver (Receptor):**
  El repositorio actúa como
  receptor que conoce cómo
  realizar las operaciones
  reales en la base de datos.
end note

' ============================================================================
' ENTIDAD
' ============================================================================
class WorkOrder {
    +id: string
    +guideNumber: string
    +currentStatus: OrderStatus
    --
    +canTransitionTo(next): boolean
}

' ============================================================================
' RELACIONES
' ============================================================================
WorkOrderRoutes --> WorkOrderInvoker : "delega ejecución"
WorkOrderRoutes --> WorkOrderCommandFactory : "crea comandos"

WorkOrderInvoker --> IWorkOrderCommand : "ejecuta"
WorkOrderInvoker o-- IWorkOrderCommand : "historial"

IUndoableCommand --|> IWorkOrderCommand

TransitionStatusCommand ..|> IUndoableCommand
AssignTechnicianCommand ..|> IUndoableCommand
RegisterExitCommand ..|> IWorkOrderCommand
AddPhotoCommand ..|> IWorkOrderCommand

WorkOrderCommandFactory ..> TransitionStatusCommand : "crea"
WorkOrderCommandFactory ..> AssignTechnicianCommand : "crea"
WorkOrderCommandFactory ..> RegisterExitCommand : "crea"
WorkOrderCommandFactory ..> AddPhotoCommand : "crea"

WorkOrderCommandFactory --> IWorkOrderRepository : "inyecta"

TransitionStatusCommand --> IWorkOrderRepository : "usa"
AssignTechnicianCommand --> IWorkOrderRepository : "usa"
RegisterExitCommand --> IWorkOrderRepository : "usa"
AddPhotoCommand --> IWorkOrderRepository : "usa"

TransitionStatusCommand ..> WorkOrder : "retorna"
AssignTechnicianCommand ..> WorkOrder : "retorna"
RegisterExitCommand ..> WorkOrder : "retorna"
AddPhotoCommand ..> WorkOrder : "retorna"

' ============================================================================
' NOTA DE BENEFICIOS
' ============================================================================
note as N1
  **Beneficios del Patrón Command:**
  
  ✓ **Desacoplamiento**: El cliente no conoce cómo se ejecutan las operaciones
  ✓ **Historial/Auditoría**: Cada comando se registra con timestamp
  ✓ **Undo/Redo**: Comandos reversibles permiten deshacer cambios
  ✓ **Extensibilidad**: Nuevos comandos se agregan sin modificar código existente
  ✓ **Single Responsibility**: Cada comando tiene una única responsabilidad
  ✓ **Testabilidad**: Comandos se pueden testear de forma aislada
end note

@enduml
